scratch/

# GPL engines must not come back. libXray.aar embedded github.com/sagernet/sing
# (GPL-3.0-or-later) and was removed, along with libbox.aar and the sing-box-*
# binaries. Do not download them and do not put them on the Gradle classpath:
# a copyleft dependency breaks the iOS build, because the App Store terms are
# incompatible with GPL-3.0 regardless of whether the app is paid.
mobile/android/app/libs/*.aar

# hysteria-client.aar is a build product, not a committed artifact.
# build-aar.sh produces it; in CI a single hy2bind-aar job builds it and passes
# it to the jobs that link it as an artifact. iOS never committed
# Hy2bind.xcframework either. The .jar is the sources archive gomobile writes
# next to it, and .source-hash records which hy2bind source the archive was
# built from, so build-sideload.ps1 can refuse a stale one.
mobile/android/app/libs/*.jar
mobile/android/app/libs/*.source-hash

# Flutter writes absolute paths into these when it resolves plugins.
mobile/windows/flutter/ephemeral/
